---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import Byline from "../components/Byline.astro";
import LegalNote from "../components/LegalNote.astro";
import { LINKS, CANON_PATHS, linkClass, ext } from "../lib/links";
import { withBase } from "../lib/base";

const path = "/sell-through-vs-search-intent";
const crumbs = [
  { name: "Home", path: "/" },
  { name: "What sold vs what they asked", path },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="What sold is not what they asked for | FFL Intel"
  description="A zero-hit search never becomes a unit. It still happened. That is the number a closed period cannot see."
  path={path}
  ogImagePath={CANON_PATHS.desk}
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-12 sm:py-14">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-sky-400 mb-3">
      The ask
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white text-balance mb-4">
      What sold is not what they asked for
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-zinc-300 mb-6">
      Sell-through is a receipt. Intent is a sentence. Mixing them is how you
      stock last year’s winner and miss this week’s hole.
    </p>
    <Byline dateLabel="August 13, 2026" read="6 min" />

    <figure class="mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800">
      <img
        src={withBase(CANON_PATHS.desk)}
        alt="Betsy at the desk"
        width="1280"
        height="720"
        class="w-full"
      />
    </figure>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.7] text-zinc-300 font-serif">
      <p>
        I like a register. I do not worship it. A unit that rang is true. A
        search that returned nothing is also true. Only one of those shows up
        in a same-store index.
      </p>
      <p>
        The ask is messy on purpose. People type slang, the wrong caliber
        punctuation, a model that is not on any participating feed. That is
        still a signal. If your website cannot see it, you will hear about it
        from the counter — late.
      </p>
      <p>
        Coriolis packages that ask for brands as Brand Intelligence. Dealers
        get the store-scoped version free on GunSearchAgent. This desk does not
        sell either. It exists so the trade stops calling every chart “demand.”
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href={LINKS.fortress} class={linkClass} {...ext}>The two factories</a>
        {" · "}
        <a href={LINKS.gsa} class={linkClass} {...ext}>Free sensor</a>
        {" · "}
        <a href={LINKS.brandIntel} class={linkClass} {...ext}
          >Brand Intelligence</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-10"><LegalNote /></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
